note right of CallAudioDeviceModule
  Bridges libwebrtc's audio pipeline to Qt
  Multimedia — libwebrtc has no pluggable
  "push samples into an AudioSource" API,
  only this device-module interface (issue #46).

  Capture is push-style: whoever owns real
  microphone PCM (future CallAudioSource,
  issue #46 Phase 3) calls pushCapturedAudio()
  whenever a buffer is ready; forwarded to
  AudioTransport::RecordedDataIsAvailable()
  while StartRecording() is active.

  Playout is pull-style but WebRTC does not
  drive the timing itself: this class runs its
  own ~10ms std::thread loop calling
  AudioTransport::NeedMorePlayData() and
  forwards decoded PCM to a caller-supplied
  PlayoutSink callback — invoked on that
  thread, NOT the Qt GUI thread. First-pass
  simplification, not yet tuned for glitch-free
  playback under real load; a caller touching
  Qt objects from the sink must marshal back
  itself (e.g. QMetaObject::invokeMethod with
  Qt::QueuedConnection).
end note

